      "content": "The Fourier Transform acts like a radar that probes your signal with pure sine waves to find the specific ones that match its internal rhythm. Instead of thinking in time, it rewrites your signal as a colorful palette of frequencies, showing you exactly how much of each \"note\" is present. This is why it feels like a magic trick: it reveals hidden patterns and noise that are invisible when you just look at the raw waveform.",
